 {"id":"fabro-5e09","title":"Develop planner: pick only seeds assigned to fabro (sd ready --assignee fabro) — deterministic line/user ownership split","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:16:32.837Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:07:20.678Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"GRILL SETTLED 2026-09-07 (user decisions in session):\n\nDECIDED: (D1) The assignee filter for the develop workflow is APPROVED — 'sd ready --assignee fabro' becomes the planner's candidate source. (D2) The REVISOR ASSIGNS NOBODY: filing seeds is its job, ownership is NOT — revisor-filed seeds land UNASSIGNED in the backlog. (D3) Who executes a seed is decided JOINTLY by user + agent (cycle report / grill / chat is the forum; the agent's @fabro assignment is a proposal the user can veto by reassigning anytime). (D4) Fail-closed default (Opt-in): nothing belongs to the line until @fabro is explicitly set. (D5) Emergency channel stays as the standing user directive: when the line/engine is DOWN the agent repairs directly with the user's knowledge (no seed picker involved); the seed is filed retroactively for documentation. No emergency self-service class exists for the revisor or the line.\n\nMECHANISM (line implements, from D1): (1) develop planner prompt candidate source: 'sd ready --assignee fabro --limit 200' (CLI pre-filters — the LLM never sees unassigned/user-owned seeds); (2) goal fast-path honors a named seed id ONLY when assignee is fabro; (3) claim: 'sd update <id> --status in_progress --assignee fabro'; (4) Tracker-empty on the filtered view = legitimate end of work (park) — while the backlog is unassigned the line does NOTHING rather than something; (5) docs/agents/issue-tracker.md documents: assignee is the ownership switch; filers (agent, revisor) file UNASSIGNED; assignment is a joint user+agent decision recorded in the cycle report; (6) revisor seed-intake prompt: remove any language implying the revisor decides execution — it only files.\n\nOWNERSHIP